  "registry_T4_chapter_digests": [
    {
      "chapter_id": "wh_ch01",
      "chapter_rolling_summary": "Lockwood visits his landlord Heathcliff at Wuthering Heights and is struck by the house’s isolation, the harsh household, and Heathcliff’s reserved, suspicious manner. After a tense first reception, the dogs attack Lockwood, Joseph and a kitchen servant restore order, and Heathcliff eventually softens enough to offer wine and conversation. Lockwood leaves intrigued, deciding to visit again despite Heathcliff’s obvious dislike of company.",
